  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance for Vulnerable Earthquake Victims in Khoy, Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 28 January 2023, a 5.9 magnitude earthquake hit Khoy, Iran, affecting over 130,000 people. The affected individuals were relocated to emergency camps managed by the Iranian Red Crescent Society (IRCS) and local authorities. The National Disaster Management Organization (NDMO) is leading the coordination of the humanitarian response, with support from the IRCS and the Ministry of Interior. To assist the affected population, the IRCS has provided relief items and medical services to vulnerable families. The NDMO sought help from the UN, leading to IOM collaborating with local authorities to provide multi-purpose cash assistance to 4,900 individuals. This support enables them to access essential goods and meet basic needs in a secure and dignified manner. IOM is working with local banks to distribute prepaid cards, allowing beneficiaries to withdraw cash or make payments for goods and services. Beneficiary selection prioritizes the most vulnerable, including women, girls, children, older people, and individuals with disabilities. Additionally, IOM is providing power generators and a training on disaster risk reduction and management topics to support the NDMO&apos;s efforts in meeting the needs in earthquake-affected villages.</narrative>
  </description>
